---
description: BirthdayPartyPilot iOS architecture and verification requirements
alwaysApply: true
---

- Keep SwiftUI views declarative and lightweight.
- Put planning and execution logic in the agent layer.
- Prefer explicit state transitions over loosely related Boolean flags.
- Every new behavior must have a focused test.
- Build after meaningful implementation changes.
- Run the closest relevant tests.
- Do not rewrite unrelated working code.
- Report build errors instead of hiding them.
- Ask before adding dependencies or changing architecture.